# L §3.3: "Allowed: rate ± rate of one period (a reference rate plus a margin), rate × num, and comparisons
# within one period."  5.85 %/year + 1 %/year = 6.85 %/year; L §5.18: "A rate prints as a decimal with its
# period (0.076 /year) ... never as %": 0.0685 /year.  rate × num: 5.85 %/year × 2 = 0.117 /year.
# L §3.2: "21 %/year * 1 month is 1.75 %", i.e. the num 0.0175.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
unit hour "godzina"

input wibor: rate
input margin: rate
input x: num
input r21: rate

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wibor = 5.85 %/year
  margin = 1 %/year
  x = 2
  r21 = 21 %/year

ask q1: wibor + margin, wibor * x, wibor > margin, r21 * 1 month
=== expect
q1: (0.0685 /year, 0.117 /year, true, 0.0175)
  cut 2026-01-01
